\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.9}{\ignorespaces Parallel binary search with $m = 7$ events, so every range starts as $[0, 8]$ (8 means ``never''). In each round the queries are checked in order of their middles during a single replay of the events; ``yes'' means connected after \emph  {mid} events. After round 4 every range is a single value; for $q_3$ it is $[1, 1]$.}}{104}{figure.caption.139}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pbs}{{8.9}{104}{Parallel binary search with $m = 7$ events, so every range starts as $[0, 8]$ (8 means ``never''). In each round the queries are checked in order of their middles during a single replay of the events; ``yes'' means connected after \emph {mid} events. After round 4 every range is a single value; for $q_3$ it is $[1, 1]$}{figure.caption.139}{}}
